How does ECMP help? (EMCP 역할)
Splits traffic across equal-cost paths, preventing concentration
동일 비용 경로가 여러개일 때 트래픽을 나눠서 집중 현상 완화

Why did you use a directed graph instead of an undirected graph?( 왜 방향성 그래프 사용했는지)
Because in real networks, links in opposite directions can have different capacities or cost.

What algorithm does nx.shortest_path use iternally? (nx.shortest_path가 무슨 알고리즘 쓰는지)
It uses Dijkstra's algorithm, which finds the path with the minimum total weight from source to destination.

What are the limitations of shortest-path routing in this simulation? (최단거리 라우팅의 한계)
It doesn't account for current congestion. The path is chosen based on static weights only, so it can still route traffic onto an already overloaded link.

Why does B->D already show 140% utilization before any failure? (왜 B->D 경로가 140% 사용률인지)
Because all four demands happen to route through B, and three of them continue to D. That puts 7 on a 5 link, resulting in 140% utilization

Does increasing the weight of B->D fully solve the congestion problem? (B->D 경로 가중치를 높이는 것만으로 문제 해결되는지)
It helps redistribute traffic, but whether it fully resolves the issue depends on the new maximum utilization after rerouting. The simulation shows improvement, but the network may still have bottlenecks

Why does removing B->D actually reduce the maximum utilization? (왜 B->D 경로 삭제가 사용률을 줄여주는지)
Without B->D, traffic is forced to reroute through C->D, which has higher capacity. This spreads the load more evenly and reduces the peak utilization.

How do you define a critical scenario in double-link failures? (double failure에서 critical scenario 가 뭔지)
A scenario is critical if at least one demand becomes unreachable, or if any remaining link's utilization exceeds 100%



